# Run-time artifacts stay out of the repository. Evidence hashes and
# verdicts are transcribed into M1_TIER2_EVIDENCE.md instead; receipts and
# logs travel as attachments to the milestone record, not as commits.
#
# infra/.terraform.lock.hcl is deliberately NOT listed here: it pins the
# hashicorp/aws provider version (6.60.0) the recorded evidence was
# actually generated against. Without it, a fresh `terraform init` on a
# later checkout resolves whatever the current latest 5.x/6.x/7.x provider
# happens to be -- against the open `>= 5.0` constraint in versions.tf --
# and a future run could produce different plan JSON, or fail outright
# after a breaking provider release, for reasons that have nothing to do
# with ChangeSafe. Commit it and let a future re-run bump it deliberately.
evidence/
infra/.terraform/
infra/terraform.tfstate
infra/terraform.tfstate.backup
infra/terraform.tfvars
*.tfplan
